{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexJonesMarkovArchimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexJonesMarkovArchimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexJonesMarkov"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_has_no_classical_leading_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_has_no_classical_leading_value","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkovArchimedean.lean#L62-L79","doc":"**The substitution factor has no classical leading value**, which is why the\n`≈ 10⁴`-order claim this file used to carry is withdrawn rather than re-scoped.\n\n`substitutionRateFactor_denominator_vanishes_numerator_does_not` gives the reason at\n`q = 1`: `s²(1) = 0` while `W(1)² = 1/16`. Here is the archimedean consequence at the\nanchor — the factor is `≈ 129.4`, i.e. `|W|²/s²` and *not* `|W|²/s⁴`, and it is nowhere\nnear any multiple of `couplingRatio_one`'s `−96`. `−96` is the classical value of\n`(J − 1)/s²`, a ratio whose numerator vanishes (`V_K(1) = 1` for every knot); this one's\ndoes not, so the two are not comparable. Bean `qou-xql6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio_near_q0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio_near_q0","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkovArchimedean.lean#L52-L60","doc":"**The ratio runs.** At the proton pin the exact ratio `−G₈G₁₂/q¹⁹` has already fallen\nfrom its classical value `−96` (`couplingRatio_one`) to `≈ −37.0915`. Since the two\ncouplings differ by a *function*, no constant relates them — this is the numerical face of\n`couplingRatio_not_constant`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}